gain, I can form a Pung. But since I'm discarding it, maybe it's better to keep W2 if possible.\n\nDiscarding B1: I have B1 and B8. Discarding B1 might be safe since I have B8. Maybe not part of any melds.\n\nDiscarding W4: I have W4. If I discard it, someone might take it for a Chow. But I don't have W3 and W5? Wait, I have W3 and W5. So if someone discards W4, I can Chi for 3-4-5. But I'm the one discarding W4 here. So maybe it's a good idea to discard W4 if I don't need it for my own melds.\n\nDiscarding W8: I have W8. If I discard it, someone might take it for a Chow. But I don't have W7 and W9. Wait, the player across has a meld of W7, W8, W9. So if I discard W8, they already have that, so maybe no one else needs it. So it's a safe discard.\n\nDiscarding T5: I have T5. If I discard it, maybe someone can use it. But I don't have T4 and T6. T6 is already out (the previous player has a Kong of B6). So maybe safe.\n\nDiscarding B8: I have B8. If I discard it, maybe someone can use it in a Chow. But I don't have B7 and B9. Wait, B7 has 3 left, B9 has 4. So if someone has B7 and B9, they might need B8. But I'm discarding B8, which could be useful for them. So maybe not safe.\n\nDiscarding T1: I have T1. If I discard it, someone might take it for a Chow. But I have T2. If they discard T3, I can Chi. But I'm discarding T1 now. So maybe safe.\n\nDiscarding T8: I have T8. If I discard it, someone might take it for a Chow. But I don't have T7 and T9. T7 is in the player across's meld. So maybe safe.\n\nNow, considering the current hand, I have a lot of tiles in different suits. Maybe I should try to form a hand that can have multiple melds. Let's see:\n\nLooking at the Characters suit: W1, W2, W3, W4, W5. These can form 123 (Chow), 45x (needs 6?), but I have W8. Not sure. Maybe 123, 456 (but I don't have W6). Alternatively, 123, 45x (maybe not). Or maybe form Pungs? I have one of each, so not possible.\n\nIn Dots: T1, T2, T5, T8, T9, T9. Maybe 123 (needs T3), but I don't 