Maybe T1-2-3? But I have T1 and T2 but not T3. Or T5-6-7? No T6. Hmm. Maybe not enough chows. So All Chows might not be possible.\n\nWhat about Full Flush? That's all tiles in one suit. My hand has multiple suits, so no.\n\nLooking for other patterns. Maybe All Simples? All Simples requires no terminals or honors. I have W1, T1, T9, B1, B8, which are terminals. So that's not applicable.\n\nWhat about Outside Hand? Each meld and pair must have terminals or honors. Let's see. If I can form four melds with terminals and a pair. For example, W1-2-3 (chow, but 2 is a middle tile), but not sure. Maybe if I discard some tiles to form pungs or chows with terminals.\n\nAlternatively, maybe forming a concealed hand with All Chows. Let's see. If I can form four chows and a pair. Let me check again:\n\n- W1-2-3 (chow)\n- T7-8-9 (chow)\n- Then, maybe T1-2-3? But I have T1 and T2, but no T3. So no.\n- W4-5? Need a third tile for a chow. Not possible.\n- T5 is a single. Maybe T5-7-8? Not consecutive. Hmm. Not enough.\n\nAnother angle: what if I discard a tile to form a kong or pung? Wait, my melds are empty, so all are concealed. Maybe if I can form a pung or kong by drawing or discarding. For example, I have two T9s. If I can get another T9, that would form a pung. But looking at the unshown tiles, T9 has 3 remaining. So if I can draw a T9, that's a pung. But I need to decide which tile to discard to maximize chances.\n\nAlternatively, maybe forming a concealed kong. But I don't have four of any tile. The only tile with two is T9. So not possible yet.\n\nWhat about the scoring patterns that might be achievable. Let's look at the 8-point patterns. For example, Chicken Hand is a low-point hand, but I need to check if my current hand is worth zero. Wait, Chicken Hand is when the hand would otherwise be zero points. But I need to see if my current hand has any scoring. For example, if I have All Chows, but I don't. Or All Pungs, but I don't. Maybe not. But this seems risky.\n\nAnothe